WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.570
Week 4: Identity, Origin, Numbers, and Time. state origin and profession exchange contact numbers tell dates and times

2
00:00:08.570 --> 00:00:16.201
Form and meaning. Ser for identity and origin; cardinal numbers; dates; telling time with es la and son las.

3
00:00:16.201 --> 00:00:36.998
Model set. Soy de los Estados Unidos. Mi apellido es Clark. Hoy es el diecinueve de julio. Son las tres y cuarto. ¿A qué hora es la reunión? I am from the United States. My last name is Clark. Today is July nineteenth. It is a quarter past three. What time is the meeting?

4
00:00:36.998 --> 00:00:47.128
Contrastive practice. Change the person, time, number, or level of formality in each model. Preserve the communicative purpose while the grammar changes.

5
00:00:47.128 --> 00:00:59.989
Production check. Say one original sentence for each function: state origin and profession; exchange contact numbers; tell dates and times. Then write it and compare the spoken and written forms.

6
00:00:59.989 --> 00:01:21.553
Model language. Soy de los Estados Unidos. — I am from the United States. Mi apellido es Clark. — My last name is Clark. Hoy es el diecinueve de julio. — Today is July nineteenth. Son las tres y cuarto. — It is a quarter past three. ¿A qué hora es la reunión? — What time is the meeting?

7
00:01:21.553 --> 00:01:31.302
Check your readiness. Explain the core idea. Produce an original example. Complete the section assessment at 85% or higher.
